title: Judiciary Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: justice_minister_party == "PSOE" and judiciary_timer = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; judiciary_timer += 6
card-image: img/portraits/RadbruchGustav.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Judiciary Reform

The Judiciary is one of the most <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> institutions inherited from the monarchy, along with the officer corps. Many judges have held their posts since before 1931, and are hostile to the Republic in all but name - handing down light sentences to monarchist plotters and Falangist street violence, while ruthlessly persecuting strikers and anarchists for lesser offenses.

[? if judicial_reform <= 0 : There is great demand in our membership for a purge of the judiciary, though this may bring us into collision with our republican coalition partners, who are wary of anything that smells of arbitrary power. ?]
[? if judicial_reform == 1 : We have started down the path of judicial reform through the new Tribunal de Garantías Constitucionales. While some of the most reactionary and biased judges have been replaced, many still remain. More should be done. ?]
[? if judicial_reform >= 2 : We have substantially reformed the judiciary. At the very least, the courts will no longer actively obstruct our attempts to prosecute crimes committed by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. ?]

- @reform: Carry out a substantial purge of the judiciary.
- @minor_reforms: Carry out minor judicial reforms.
- @as_is: Leave the judiciary as it is.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; democratization += 2; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; industrial_psoe += 5*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent); coup_progress += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if historical_mode; izq_rep_relation += 1.5; president_angry += 5

We investigate judges who have shown biased or corrupt behavior through the new Tribunal de Garantías Constitucionales, and remove them, replacing them with jurists committed to the Republic. This raises considerable ire in conservative circles, including within our own coalition.

@minor_reforms
on-arrival: democratization += 1; industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 1; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent); judiciary_timer += 6; izq_rep_relation += 0.5

We try to remove the most obviously biased and corrupt judges, while leaving most of the system intact. It is slow work reforming the judiciary.

@as_is
go-to: root
